Fix bury count inflation on WAL replay (issue #67; upstream bug, unfixed in
v1.13 and on master).

When persistence is enabled (-b <dir>), prot_replay restores each buried job
from the WAL by calling bury_job(), which unconditionally increments
j->r.bury_ct. readrec() has already restored the job's true bury count from
the WAL record, so every daemon restart reported one extra bury in stats-job.

Preserve the recovered bury count across the bury_job() call during replay.
bury_job() is left unchanged because its other update_store = 0 callers
(out-of-memory buries) are real buries that must still be counted.

--- a/prot.c
+++ b/prot.c
@@ -2352,7 +2352,11 @@
         int64 delay = 0;
         switch (j->r.state) {
         case Buried: {
+            /* The WAL record already holds the job's bury count; restoring
+             * it is not a new bury. */
+            uint32 bury_ct = j->r.bury_ct;
             bury_job(s, j, 0);
+            j->r.bury_ct = bury_ct;
             break;
         }
         case Delayed:
